==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Doge]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Snache]]s spawn, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Those Guys]] spawn after 40 seconds<sup>1,200f</sup>, delay 3~20 seconds<sup>90f~600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Teacher Bear]]s spawn, delay 40~53.33 seconds<sup>1,200f~1,600f</sup>.
*Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**Infinite [[B.B.Bunny|B.B.Bunnies]] spawn, delay 3~6 seconds<sup>90f~180f</sup>.
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.
**1 [[Teacher Bear]] spawns.
*When the base reaches 80% HP:
**Infinite [[Doge Dark]]s spawn, delay 8~12 seconds<sup>240f~360f</sup>.

==Strategy==
Use long-ranged units such as [[Lizard Cat (Normal Cat)|Dragon Cat]] or [[Figure Skating Cats (Super Rare Cat)|Drama Cats]] against the Teacher Bears. [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Ring Girl Cat]] is a great option for dealing with the Doge Darks, but be wary of her low speed and range.

If you have a [[:Category:Long Distance Cats|Long Distance]] unit, you can use it to hit the Teacher Bears while they are shielded by peons. If you have [[Bahamut Cat (Special Cat)|Crazed Bahamut Cat]], use him to deal heavy damage to the Teacher Bears and Doge Darks, but be sure to meatshield constantly so that the Teacher Bears do not get close enough to hit him.

Short-ranged cats can be useful for clearing out Doge Darks despite being more vulnerable to the Teacher Bears' attacks. [[Salon Cat (Rare Cat)|Paris Cat]] is good at fending off the peons, but then you run the risk of a whole stack of them being wiped out by Teacher Bears due to them having the same range.

==Trivia==
*Seaweed Shallows' Japanese name, Tengusa Island (テングサ島), is a reference to the real-world [[wikipedia:Amakusa|Amakusa islands]] (天草諸島). The connection is that 天草 (Amakusa) can also be read as ''tengusa'', which refers to any of the red algae of the genus ''[[wikipedia:Gelidium|Gelidium]]''.

